        <mxCell id="i75__r1__c1" value="Top level of a CAN protocol controller for microcontroller-style hosts. It joins the host bus to an internal register file, a bit-timing generator and a frame-processing engine, and exposes the serial CAN receive and transmit lines, an interrupt output, a bus-off status output and a programmable clock output. In this configuration the host uses a multiplexed address/data bus with separate address-latch, read and write strobes and a chip-select input." style="shape=partialRectangle;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;connectable=0;fillColor=none;strokeColor=#000000;strokeWidth=1;overflow=hidden;pointerEvents=1;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;spacing=4;fontSize=18;fontColor=#000000;" vertex="1" parent="i75__r1" vlsit_native_table="1">
